  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/229086940",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/1457#issuecomment-229086940",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/1457",
    "id": 229086940,
    "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyOTA4Njk0MA==",
    "user": {
      "login": "beidson",
      "id": 13395822,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzk1ODIy",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13395822?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/beidson",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/beidson/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2016-06-28T15:32:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-28T15:32:56Z",
    "body": "> do you actually use that in your implementation? Or do you have a reasonable lifetime model plus OOM clauses (which the specification already grants for all features).\n\nWe could utilize the current clause AND have a \"reasonable lifetime model plus OOM clauses\", so this \"OR\" question is a false choice.\n\nUser experience extends to the user's entire software and hardware environment, not just a web page they're currently viewing. Also, running OOM is not the only resource constraint that might come up.\n\nThis is a 100% hypothetical example that we have not implemented, but it is realistc - If the battery on a user's iPhone is running low, and especially if the user has turned on \"Low Power Mode\", we might want to take drastic steps to keep a whole CPU core idle as well as avoid context switches by sharing one core, so we might want to end the worker.\n\nIf pressed, I'm sure I can come up with other realistic scenarios supported by the current general language that are not supported by the more specific OOM clause.\n\nAnd then, even after I came up with that list, the current clause is a safety valve against unforeseen scenarios whereas the OOM clause is not.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/229086940/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
