    "created_at": "2016-06-28T16:42:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-28T16:42:27Z",
    "body": "Thanks. Please also talk to the folks implementing `SharedArrayBuffer` and consider that as web pages start to move updating their tree into workers, killing arbitrary workers is the same as killing the current tab.\n\nOur point of view is that killing the threads independent from the browsing context they are spawn from does not gain you much and actually leads to a bunch of subtle issues.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
