    "body": "The change looks good, and thanks very much to Apple for getting back to us.\r\n\r\n@annevk, can you help me understand why we have two algorithms in the first place, and why \"terminate\" is the one we want to keep? The differences seem to be that \"kill\" is allowed to wait a user-agent defined amount of time, and \"terminate\" empties the port message queue. I'm really confused why these are different in the current spec, and I'd feel better about changing the spec if I understood the original spec.",
