    "updated_at": "2017-04-18T19:01:31Z",
    "body": "I think kill a worker defines to wait to avoid exposing too much details as to why it's happening. Whereas terminate is the direct result of invoking `terminate()`. Though I think in practice the latter can also end up having to wait a bit due to parallelism. Anyway, that's my speculation, I can't say for sure. There's definitely room for future cleanup here.",
